[h1]Worker Optimizer[/h1]
[b]TL;DR:[/b] Auto-assign workers with one click, or enable a schedule at day start or every 5, 10 or 15 real-time minutes. Keep a builder reserve and choose which workplaces matter most.

Worker Optimizer assigns eligible residents using guild specialties, productivity and your priorities. It plans minimum operating crews before adding extra workers, subject to eligibility and the available workforce.

[list]
[*][b]General:[/b] set a builder reserve of 0-100 eligible residents (default: 1), choose an assignment mode and configure automatic runs.
[*][b]Priorities:[/b] search buildings, adjust categories and override individual building types. Choose strict priorities or priority-weighted productivity.
[*][b]Logbook:[/b] inspect run history, assignment changes and reported reasons for unfilled workplaces.
[*][b]Protected workers:[/b] workers in paused or unsupported buildings keep their assignments.
[*][b]17 game languages:[/b] follows the game's language automatically, with English fallback.
[/list]

[h2]Quick start[/h2]
Subscribe, let Steam download, then restart the game. Remove any separate local WorkerOptimizer installation first.
Click the [b]arrow at the lower left[/b] to run. The gear opens [b]General, Priorities and Logbook[/b]; the logbook button opens history directly. [b]Ctrl + Alt + O[/b] shows or hides the controls, and the shortcut can be changed in General.

Automatic assignment is [b]off by default[/b]. Minute intervals count real time, including pauses. Assignment processing waits until the game resumes; missed intervals do not accumulate into repeated runs.

The start button stays locked while a request is active. Extra clicks do not restart or cancel it. There is no player cancellation or automatic undo of completed assignments.

[b]v0.2.0:[/b] automated checks and the final in-game test passed. Large settlements, complex workplace arrangements and presentation in every language still need broader testing. Try a separate test save before using it in an established settlement.

